This is the GREEN-phase evidence for the Sprint-4 Phase-3 contract-review findings fix round
(FIND-001, FIND-002).

Fix: _modeb_ratio_n() and _modeb_next_wake_count() now explicitly base-10-force every ratio/counter
digit string via "$((10#$digits))" BEFORE it is ever used in bash arithmetic, so a leading-zero
shape (e.g. "08", "09", "1-in-08") is correctly normalized to its decimal value (never
octal-misparsed, never a raw "value too great for base" crash) instead of relying on the old
"^[0-9]+$" regex alone. A normalization failure (belt-and-suspenders; cannot occur for a
regex-filtered pure-digit string within bash's integer range) fails closed to Mode A, same as every
other REQ-25 malformed case. The SAME guard is also applied, identically, right before the modulo at
the AUTONOMY branch (previously line ~133, the FIND-002 gap) -- not just at the _modeb_ratio_n
"-eq 0" check (previously line ~105) -- so the fail-closed behavior is now deliberate and
consistent at every arithmetic site, not incidental at one and absent at the other.

